. The company operates through three segments: Pharma, Beauty, and Closures. It provides dispensing pumps used to dispense sprays, liquids, or lotions from non-pressurized containers; fine-mist pumps for pharmaceutical and fragrance applications; and lotion pumps for viscous formulations, as well as closures, such as dispensing and non-dispensing solutions that enable product delivery without removal of the cap and used across various consumer end markets. The company also offers aerosol valves used in pressurized containers and continuous spray and metered-dose valves for pharmaceutical, personal care, and household applications; elastomeric primary packaging components; active material science solutions; and digital health solutions. The company primarily sells its products and services in Asia, Europe, Latin America, and North America. AptarGroup, Inc. was incorporated in 1992 and is headquartered in Crystal Lake, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gael  Touya | CEO, President & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 14K people. Revenue per employee of $270K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $21K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["AptarGroup, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $9.0B market cap on $3.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 29%.","The business throws off $300M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.45\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.5\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 153% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.5315068572696047},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Healthcare peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","32 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"AptarGroup (ATR) Lifts Its Dividend Following Earnings, Is It Still 11% Below Fair Value?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/aptargroup-atr-lifts-dividend-following-002230160.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793665350.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.947,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"Investing in AptarGroup (ATR)? Don't Miss Assessing Its International Revenue Trends","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020428/investing-in-aptargroup-atr-don-t-miss-assessing-its-international-revenue-trends?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_international_revenues-3020428","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793625304.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.114,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Atrium Therapeutics to Present Nonclinical Data Showing ATR 1072 Reversed and Improved Features of PRKAG2 Syndrome During HCMS at AHA Scientific Sessions 2026","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/atrium-therapeutics-to-present-nonclinical-data-showing-atr-1072-reversed-and-improved-featu